 "result": "Rules are recorded as deferred callbacks on the bundle, then replayed against the app at registration.\n\n**Recording (before registration)**\n- `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`) checks the endpoint and view names for dots, then calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`. The `route` decorator in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:344` ends up here.\n- `Bundle.record` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:224`) appends the callback to `self.deferred_functions`.\n\n**Registration**\n1. `Tessel.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)` at line 596.\n2. `Bundle.register` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:273`):\n   - It stores the bundle in `app.bundles[name]`.\n   - It builds the state with `Bundle.make_setup_state` (line 246), which returns a `BundleSetupState`.\n   - It loops `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (line 334).\n   - It also registers the static route via `state.attach_route_rule` (line 324).\n   - It recurses into nested bundles at line 377.\n3. `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:87`) applies the URL prefix, subdomain and URL defaults, and prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.`. It then calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`.\n4. `App.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`) normalizes the methods, builds `url_rule_class(...)`, and calls `self.url_map.add(rule_obj)` at line 654. It also stores the view in `self.view_functions[endpoint]`.",
